                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Despite being the third game, you do not need to play 1 and 2 first, and I recommend you don't. They can be fun, but they're way less polished and all the games in the series are connected pretty loosely anyways.\n\nWhile Momodora Reverie Under the Moonlight is the peak of the series, this game is still very worth playing regardless, and for only $2, it's a great way to see if the series is for you. It has more of a retro feel than it's successor, which makes it refreshing to play, even if you've had your fill of the sequel.",
